# SABOTAGE: MG-08 (ADR-049 mutation ledger) — `Samen.Pii.WriteGuard.plaintext_write?/2`
# is WIDENED so a round-tripping `%Masked{}` counts as operator-authored PLAINTEXT. An
# operator who re-submits the very value they were SHOWN (`••••`, the masked struct the
# vault-routed column presents on every read) is then refused under MC-1 / Invariant L1 as
# if they had typed the tenant's PII themselves.
#
# The OVER-refusal direction again, and the reason it needs its own red: every shipped
# RP-L1 test writes genuine plaintext, so they all stay green — the guard gets STRICTER.
# What breaks is the operator plane's ordinary form round-trip: any operator edit of a
# PII-bearing row that re-sends the masked field is refused.
#
# Flips the named MG-08 red. The anti-tautology CONTROL stays green — genuine operator
# plaintext into the SAME field is still refused with "no-operator-plaintext-write" and the
# stored token is unchanged — so the red fails because the `%Masked{}` arm was widened, not
# because the guard, the plane detection or the vault write path broke. MG-09's and MG-10's
# reds (the raw-token and explicit-nil arms) also stay green: this patch touches ONE clause.
#
# One case clause, one literal. Touches write_guard.ex ALONE.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/hardening/pii_write_guard_fail_closed_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: MG-08: an OPERATOR re-setting the %Masked{} value they were shown is ALLOWED
diff --git a/samen_core/lib/samen/pii/write_guard.ex b/samen_core/lib/samen/pii/write_guard.ex
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/pii/write_guard.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/pii/write_guard.ex
@@ -116,7 +116,7 @@ defmodule Samen.Pii.WriteGuard do
   # explicit nil (clear), a round-tripping %Masked{}, or a raw vt_* token are NOT writes.
   defp plaintext_write?(changeset, name) do
     case Ash.Changeset.fetch_change(changeset, name) do
-      {:ok, %Masked{}} -> false
+      {:ok, %Masked{}} -> true
       {:ok, "vt_" <> _} -> false
       {:ok, nil} -> false
       {:ok, _plaintext} -> true
